al  leviathan which has aux and optical in  options so i don't understand why razer  would downgrade and upgrade sure there's  bluetooth but we all know bluetooth and  pcs don't exactly have the best  relationship it does work well with your  phone for low latency music playback  though and i haven't any issues with  that yet we'll have to see how it  performs in the long run however the  katana v2 on the other hand has all  those options in addition to hdmi arc  and 65 out ports if you're into that  also a headphone port at the front of  the soundbar for easier access compared  to the v1 which is at the back something  both leviathans have none of so why  would razer limit the options i don't  know simplifying tech is great but this  is a little too much it takes away a lot  of the options the consumer has with the  katana v2 and we like options so the  katana v2 wins in this regard also the  leviathan v2 doesn't come with a remote  like the katana v1 and v2 and a lot of  original leviathan owners have been  asking for that for quite a while now  getting into aesthetics both katanas and  the violence are good looking sound bars  i mean you gotta be honest i like the  smaller form factor on the vitam v2 and  how stylish it is with its great black  textures compared to the v1 and they  come with angled feet which is a nice  touch if you need the extra elevation  the leviton v2 in comparison fits snugly  under your monitor and i honestly have  no complaints about extra realistic then  we have chroma rgb it doesn't look as  impressive compared to rgb served up by  the katana v2 which diffuses beautifully  though it needs to be set you can  customize 18 sections of the lighting  individually for the leviathan v2 and  both katanas can't do that now you got  to use the navs to change the lighting  on the leviathan but if you want to  change the lighting with your phone you  got to disconnect the leviton completely  from the pc  and to your phone via bluetooth and just  why the creative app on my phone lets  you change things up while you're  connected to your pc so we found  greatest way of connection very much  bizarre we'll get into the apps a bit  more later on okay so sound quality with  the leviton v2 you're getting two 95  millimeter full range drivers two 20  millimeter tweeters two passive radiator  drivers and a 144 millimeter subwoofer  the katana v2 meanwhile has two 63  millimeter mid-range drivers two 19  millimeter tweeters and a 165 millimeter  subwoofer and also a mic which is still  impressive that they managed to fit it  on there so to start the leviathan v2 is  honestly  pretty good it's well balanced highs are  crisp but surprisingly the base isn't as  punchy as i thought it would be given  how razer likes to tune their audio  stuff but that's also probably a new  part because you know it's well balanced  so i guess they were going for that  sound staging is wide and imaging is  somewhat detailed listening to bands  like total toe arch tremors and  periphery guitars and vocals sound crisp  and somewhat full but you're gonna need  to play around with the eq on synapse to  get the drums and bass sounding punchier  gaming wise i was playing apex legends  and i'm able to pick out where the  enemies are coming from footsteps are  detailed and so are gunshots  which makes the leviathan v2 a pretty  fun samba to have while playing games  all in all the leviathan v2 does the job  well whether you're playing music or  gaming and of course it gets loud i  don't find myself going beyond 30 of my  volume so at its most basic usage as an  under monitor audio system it succeeds  in delivering especially with thx  spatial audio it adds a little more  depth to your music and gameplay in a  way i do like what razer has done here  they've made a significant improvement  they've made a significant improvement  over the original but of course that's  relative to them now not even comparing  the leviathan v2 to the katana v2 but  the katana v1 sound is a lot more full  and warm sound staging is much wider and  imaging is more precise the leviton v2  sounds very boxed up and flat compared  to the katana v1 i'd say the leviathan  and katana v2s are on par when it comes  to how loud they can go but the katana  v2 is definitely more detailed in terms  of articulation instruments are more  pronounced than full gunshots and  explosions are punchier while footsteps  and imaging are more accurate also  turning scout mode on with the katana v2  which is an eq of sorts amps up your  entire gaming experience i'm pretty sure  audiophiles out there will get a kick  out of listening to this now  software  snaps as well synapse it's oftentimes  jankier than more software out there but  when it works it works the interface is  very simple you can switch between  stereo and thx there's a volume bar you  can choose to turn on center focus you  can even assign another audio device and  hold down the source button on the  leviathan which is actually really handy  when you want to swap out over to  headphones without having to navigate  the windows interface lastly there's the  equalizer which i've experienced some  issues with sometimes i cannot get them  to switch between the five options but  more often than not i can't for some  reason they'll probably patch it up at  some point but as of now it's not at its  best i tried the game eq option and i  was just stressed out hell the music eq  option is still the best out of the lot  or you know just customize your own the  creative app has a lot more to offer  with eq options for different games and  scenarios voice modifiers a decoder  scout mode and the sexify option which  you need to download separately  all in all it's very comprehensive back  to controlling the leviathan your phone  numb  you gotta download two separate apps  yeah to control both audio and rgb  but the creative app is all in one and  you can tweak the same exact options on  the pc app razer is probably working on  creating an all-in-one app but there's  no release date yet and that's another  point for the creative katana v2  conclusion  in terms of customization connectivity  options and performance i would avoid  the points to the katana series and i  think many of y'all out there would  choose it over leviathans despite its  bigger price tag again it should be  noted that creative is an audio company  so this is their playing field that  raises on if razer added that aux port i  honestly would not mind getting it  because it actually is a decent sambar  but of course it restricts you to your  pc if you don't mind the lack of  connectivity options the leviathan works  well enough for the casual gamer and  listener of course not all of you out  there would agree with me since this is  all based on my personal experience with  both products so if you have any  questions leave them in the comment  section down below and i'll do my best  to answer them  follow us on all our socials and if you  like this video leave a like and  subscribe to us we've got tons of videos  coming your way this is ineo and i'm  gonna go blast the shot of them  [Music]

